## GNU nano (Homebrew), set up the way it behaves on Ubuntu. Symlinked to ~/.nanorc by
## bin/apply.sh. macOS's own /usr/bin/nano is really pico: no line numbers, no colours.

## Line numbers on the left, and a scroll-position bar on the right.
set linenumbers
set indicator

## Colours per file type: every syntax Homebrew's nano ships (YAML, JSON, shell, Python,
## Markdown, Go, SQL, HTML, CSS, Makefile, nanorc, and more).
include "/opt/homebrew/share/nano/*.nanorc"

## Editing comfort.
set autoindent
set tabsize 4

## Keys that survive the Ctrl remaps of this repo. Hammerspoon turns Ctrl+X and Ctrl+C into cut
## and copy in every app, terminals included, so nano's usual Exit (^X) and Cancel (^C) never
## arrive. These two are untouched by the remaps:
##   Ctrl+S  save                          (as in any editor; nano's own default too)
##   Ctrl+Q  exit, or cancel the question nano is asking
## F2 (exit) and F3 (save) keep working as well.
bind ^S savefile main
bind ^Q cancel all
bind ^Q exit main
